  "interpretation": "At steady state, with the anti-spoof buffer filled, the median packet costs [751.4, 838.8] ms and the p95 [930.6, 1068.9] ms against a 1000 ms budget. Startup is a separate cost: 17638 ms to load the bundle, plus a first packet an order of magnitude above steady state.",
  "limitations": [
    "One machine: a 12-thread AMD CPU with onnxruntime on CPUExecutionProvider only, because the installed driver caps at CUDA 11.2 while onnxruntime-gpu needs CUDA 12. These figures do not transfer to other hardware and say nothing about a GPU deployment.",
    "One session at a time. Concurrent calls would contend for the same cores, so no throughput or multi-session claim follows from this.",
    "Measured through FastAPI's TestClient, which exercises the real ASGI app but not a real network. Wire latency, TLS and a production ASGI server are excluded.",
    "FLEURS clips are concatenated to build a continuous stream, so the audio contains joins that a real call would not. That affects what the models see, not what a packet costs."
  ],
  "conclusion": "Quote steady-state median AND p95 together with the hardware. The budget verdict above determines whether O13 can move; a median inside the budget with a p95 outside it is not a pipeline that keeps up, because the overrun packets are the ones that accumulate.",
